===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# A plant of certain species of the genus {{taxfmt|Brassica|genus}}, or of related genera (especially {{taxfmt|Sinapis alba|species}}, in the family {{taxfmt|Brassicaceae|family}}, with yellow [[flower]]s, and linear [[seed]] [[pod]]s).
#: {{syn|en|senvy<qq:obsolete>}}
# {{senseid|en|Q131748}}Powder or paste made from seeds of the mustard plant, and used as a [[condiment]] or a [[spice]].
#: {{ux|en|When the waitress brought the food, I asked whether she had any Dijon '''mustard'''.}}
# The leaves of the mustard plant, used as a [[salad]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Mustard''' and cress sandwiches.}}
# Dark [[yellow]] [[color|colour]], the colour of mustard.
#: {{color panel|e6d200}}
# One of a family of [[vesicant]]s containing one or more 2-chloroethyl (C<sub>2</sub>H<sub>4</sub>Cl) groups, commonly used in [[chemical warfare]] and [[cancer]] [[chemotherapy]].
# The [[tomalley]] of a [[crab]], which resembles the condiment.
# {{ellipsis of|en|mustard gas}}
# {{lb|en|baseball|colloquial}} [[energy#Noun|Energy]], [[power#Noun|power]] (when throwing a [[baseball#Noun|baseball]]).
#* {{quote-web|en|author=[[w:Scott Russell (commentator)|Scott Russell]]|title=Sport was the great connection for Scott Russell and his father|site=w:CBC News|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221022140052/https://www.cbc.ca/sports/scott-russell-oct21-1.6622331|date=20 October 2022|passage=He's left-handed and in his adulthood didn't have a baseball glove to call his own. He borrowed one of mine and just out of the car, still wearing his lab coat having worked an overnight shift, he taught himself to throw right-handed and put plenty of '''mustard''' on it.}}

